flowchart LR
  %% diagram: gateway-gcp
  %% PAPER DESIGN, nothing built. The AWS `gateway` block is the build record.
  %% The name line above must stay bare. publish-architecture.sh finds it with a
  %% line-anchored regex and exits if a block has no clean name, so keep any
  %% commentary on its own line and never repeat the name token inline.
  %% ---
  %% LAID OUT FOR THE SITE'S PAN/ZOOM STAGE, WHICH IS LANDSCAPE. Not for a
  %% free-scrolling page - that was an earlier, wrong assumption. site.css has
  %%   .stage{height:min(74vh,760px)}
  %% and index.html fits each diagram with
  %%   base = min(stageW/W, stageH/H) * 0.96
  %% so in a ~1050x760 stage the best aspect is 1050/760 = 1.38, and a TALL
  %% diagram is punished twice: it wastes the horizontal axis AND shrinks to fit
  %% the height. Measured on this exact content:
  %%   TB  1481 x 2187  aspect 0.68  -> fit 0.334
  %%   LR  2261 x 1556  aspect 1.45  -> fit 0.446   <- this file
  %%   AWS gateway diagram, 2563 x 2445, 1.05       -> fit 0.298
  %% Two rules follow, and the render will punish breaking either:
  %%   1. NOTHING FLOATS. An unanchored node gets its own column off to the side,
  %%      inflating one axis for no information. Every node hangs off the spine.
  %%      Do not add a node without an edge.
  %%   2. WIDE AND SHORT. Lines cap at ~40 chars so nodes stay narrow, and the
  %%      flow runs LR so extra ranks add width rather than height.
  %% Commentary that does not hang off a node belongs in the page prose beside
  %% the figure - see plan/gcp/01-deployment-and-billing-gcp.md section 7.5.

  PAPER["<b>⚠️ PAPER DESIGN — nothing built</b><br/>The AWS gateway diagram is a build record.<br/>This one is drawn from documentation only."]

  subgraph LAPTOP["Developer laptop"]
    MS["managed-settings.json<br/>forceLoginMethod · forceLoginGatewayUrl<br/><i>managed-only keys, pushed by MDM</i><br/><b>identical to the AWS deployment;<br/>only the URL differs</b>"]
    CC["<b>Claude Code</b><br/>an IdP session, and nothing else<br/><b>no GCP credential on the machine</b>"]
    MS --> CC
  end

  subgraph IDP["Google Workspace - the identity provider"]
    WS["<b>1 · 2 - sign in, session minted</b><br/>accounts.google.com · /oauth/callback<br/>scopes: openid, profile, email<br/>allowed_email_domains gates sign-in"]
    GRP["<b>⚠️ id_tokens carry no groups claim</b><br/>oidc.google_groups queries the Admin SDK<br/>via a service-account <b>key file</b> with<br/>domain-wide delegation<br/><i>without it, one policy per email domain</i><br/><i>a non-issue on Okta or Entra</i>"]
    WS --> GRP
  end

  ALB["<b>3 - reaching the gateway</b><br/>internal Application Load Balancer<br/>internal DNS name and certificate<br/><i>*.run.app is public, so /login's<br/>private-address check rejects it</i><br/><i>set trusted_proxies, or audit lines<br/>record the balancer, not the developer</i>"]

  subgraph GCP["Google Cloud - project «project» · region «region»"]
    SM["<b>Secret Manager</b> - four secrets<br/>config · jwt · oidc secret · pg url"]
    SA["<b>Service account</b> - no static keys<br/>roles/aiplatform.user<br/>ADC on Cloud Run or Workload Identity"]
    GW["<b>claude gateway</b><br/>image from Artifact Registry<br/>Cloud Run ingress internal, or GKE<br/>--timeout=3600, or streams cut at 300s<br/>Direct VPC egress to Cloud SQL<br/><i>⚠️ org policy can force the GKE track</i>"]
    PG["<b>Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL 16</b><br/>private IP · sslmode=require<br/>sessions, spend limits, audit<br/><i>boot is fail-closed after 5s</i>"]
    AP["<b>4 - inference · Agent Platform</b><br/>provider: vertex · project · region<br/>claude-opus-4-8 · claude-sonnet-4-6<br/><i>first-party ids, no us.anthropic.</i>"]
    RES["<b>Residency - three tiers</b><br/>global: no premium<br/>multi-region us or eu: <b>10%</b><br/>regional: 10%, one named region<br/><b>⚠️ regional serves Sonnet 4.6 and older</b><br/><i>one region costs models, not just 10%</i>"]
    RET["<b>Retention - unlike Bedrock</b><br/>~24h cache on by default; turn it off<br/>with disableCache on the project<br/><b>⚠️ no fail-closed, no allowed_modes,</b><br/><b>no source field, no Org Policy lock</b>"]
    SM -.-> GW
    SA -.-> GW
    GW --> PG
    GW ==> AP
    AP --> RES
    AP --> RET
  end

  POL["<b>Policy, enforced server-side</b><br/>availableModels + enforceAvailableModels<br/>permissions.deny · desktop: {}<br/>keyed on IdP group, at the managed tier<br/><b>identical to AWS - the claude binary,<br/>not the cloud</b>"]
  AUD["<b>Audit</b> - one JSON line each<br/>device.authorize · session.mint<br/>managed.serve · inference<br/><b>the only per-developer record</b> - the<br/>cloud sees one service account"]
  CAL["<b>⚠️ Cloud Audit Logs - default inverts</b><br/>prediction calls are DATA_READ, so they<br/>land in <b>Data Access logs, off by default</b><br/><i>on AWS the CloudTrail record needs no<br/>opt-in; here it must be enabled first</i>"]

  PAPER -.-> MS
  CC ==> WS
  CC ==> ALB
  ALB ==> GW
  GW --> POL
  GW --> AUD
  AP -.-> CAL

  style PAPER fill:#fff1f0,stroke:#b42318,stroke-width:3px
  style POL fill:#f6f4ff
  style AUD fill:#f6f4ff
  style CAL fill:#fff7ed
  style RES fill:#fff7ed
  style RET fill:#fff7ed
  style GRP fill:#fff7ed
